2186503653 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/29/29559fd9cbee104e92c719d4c33dd7560d2e2ab8c4f25490659b73f07350debc.png)\n\nSolve for $x$ in the figure above given that $\\angle AOC$ is complementary to $\\angle COD.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503653 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0d68be9a-8e75-5378-a88f-92da1a8cda66" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503653 #edb/ref 1074 "From the diagram, we have \n\n$$\nm\\angle AOC=x + 24^{\\circ}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\nm\\angle COD=3x.\n$$\n\n  \n\nSince $\\angle AOC$ is complementary to $\\angle COD,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+{24}^{∘})+3x & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ 4x+{24}^{∘} & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ 4x & ={66}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={16.5}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503682 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186503517 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503682 #edb/ref 1069 "q-357039" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503682 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503682 #edb/ref 1071 "If $∠C$ and $∠D$ are complementary angles and $m∠C={51}^{∘}$, find the measure of $∠D.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503682 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4b2d722a-94fe-5e1c-9243-0a6e73122040" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503682 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/a9/a910150e8bcfe1d8b4d5e16dd2244a4f5e4da7d6ad965b606293128f8595fa09.png)\n\nSince $∠C$ and $∠D$ are complementary, the sum of their measures is equal to ${90}^{∘}.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠C+m∠D & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ {51}^{∘}+m∠D & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ m∠D & ={39}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503694 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186503615 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503694 #edb/ref 1069 "q-5922" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503694 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503694 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/c4/c4ff51ad6db174c8bc6284a247f9ac6460de8b1483c211acaf68c5e8559bfaa5.png)\n\nSolve for $x$ given the figure above." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503694 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "63e22990-215d-5b0e-8964-b23a81f16703" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503694 #edb/ref 1074 "From the diagram, we have two complementary angles, so\n\n$$\n{54}^{∘}+(10x+{6}^{∘})={90}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nHence, we can solve for $x$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{54}^{∘}+(10x+{6}^{∘}) & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ 10x+{60}^{∘} & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ 10x & ={30}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={3}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503710 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186503526 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503710 #edb/ref 1069 "q-357050" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503710 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503710 #edb/ref 1071 "If $∠X$ and $∠Y$ are complementary angles and $m∠X={47}^{∘}$, then $m∠Y=${{field-1}}\n${}^{∘}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503710 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "828e982d-a9a1-585f-8390-ab20f7e96140" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503710 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/80/8079f80c1adad20a0844885f06cb56feb8fc55d8172aa154d4d2c484c3b977cc.png)\n\nSince $∠X$ and $∠Y$ are complementary, the sum of their measures is equal to ${90}^{∘}.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠X+m∠Y & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ {47}^{∘}+m∠Y & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ m∠Y & ={43}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503730 #edb/ref 1069 "e-18990" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503730 #edb/ref 1071 "The angles $\\angle a$ and $\\angle b$ are complementary angles. If $m \\angle a = 37^\\circ,$ what is the measure of $\\angle b?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503730 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b2c15979-d071-5f8a-b3a3-0e1228124d71" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503730 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/18/18d67b5d6d05c29fdf286406cdb8f1615f623c942c55d414b0655c8ac0ef242b.png)\n\nSince $\\angle a$ and $\\angle b$ are complementary, the sum of their measures is equal to $90^\\circ.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠a+m∠b & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ {37}^{∘}+m∠b & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ m∠b & ={90}^{∘}-{37}^{∘} \\\\ m∠b & ={53}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503734 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186503529 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503734 #edb/ref 1069 "q-357053" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503734 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503734 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/93/9306c9b7f6dfed945d955c27d12635bf5b1952288d5c833e22737d4c39da8ad2.png)\n\nSolve for $x$ given the figure above.\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503734 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b8987b97-dcba-5e61-82e1-c9e2d8c85a88" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503734 #edb/ref 1074 "From the diagram, we have two complementary angles, so\n\n$$\n(x+{15}^{∘})+(4x-{5}^{∘})={90}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nHence, we can solve for $x$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+{15}^{∘})+(4x-{5}^{∘}) & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ 5x+{10}^{∘} & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ 5x & ={80}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={16}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503736 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186503618 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503736 #edb/ref 1069 "q-357055" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503736 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503736 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/d3/d3356cf5182c27467cc122249c4212b81934825bfcb96d4f62489d485218a973.png)\n\nSolve for $x$ given the figure above.\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503736 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bc96f5c1-f42e-58eb-b44f-349743640f2a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503736 #edb/ref 1074 "From the diagram, we have two complementary angles, so\n\n$$\n(2x+{14}^{∘})+(4x-{8}^{∘})={90}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nHence, we can solve for $x$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2x+{14}^{∘})+(4x-{8}^{∘}) & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ 6x+{6}^{∘} & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ 6x & ={84}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={14}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503748 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186503641 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503748 #edb/ref 1069 "q-357054" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503748 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503748 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/49/490d1cc553867d48b934ad72c42fa69c355d7d8facf0999034fc6ca9e4fa7323.png)\n\nSolve for $x$ given the figure above.\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503748 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "db49ef55-d719-58c2-91e1-31736abaa714" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503748 #edb/ref 1074 "From the diagram, we have two complementary angles, so\n\n$$\n{28}^{∘}+(3x+{5}^{∘})={90}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nHence, we can solve for $x$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{28}^{∘}+(3x+{5}^{∘}) & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ 3x+{33}^{∘} & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ 3x & ={57}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={19}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521612 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186116387 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521612 #edb/ref 1061 619142 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521612 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "70f7bf88-80a0-59ab-b3a1-742cf3923640" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521612 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186521659 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521657 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186521612 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521657 #edb/ref 1061 484814 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521657 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "fab99fb7-13ba-526e-9805-8357cfddf511" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521657 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186503647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521659 #edb/ref 1064 "Now, consider the following diagram.\n\n![](images/02/02d8744bbc39ac9ed10d276071599f9008185023ebdfc3aaf97aebd498d82629.png)\n\nLet's solve for $x$ given the figure above.\n\nFrom the diagram, we have two complementary angles, so\n\n$$\n46^\\circ + (8x + 4^\\circ) = 90^\\circ.\n$$\n\nHence, we can solve for $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{46}^{∘}+(8x+{4}^{∘}) & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ 8x+{50}^{∘} & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ 8x & ={40}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={5}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521659 #edb/ref 1065 15157 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521659 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "62b39d73-2c91-59ba-9e98-44a61a98c7b4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521659 #edb/ref 1067 "Working With Diagrams" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
